From 4916e70e69b8dc4cfdb6d8811d496c3b6bab0324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HOTTY Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:37:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-dom: a box gone display: none forgets the boxes built
 under it

A box that goes display: none gets no construction of its own: its
parent constructs again and may not list it any more (an inline parent
does not), and its subtree, unstyled from then on, reports no damage,
not even a removal. So the box and its subtree kept their layout
children, anonymous blocks, inline layouts, table contexts, hoisted
out-of-flow boxes and paint trees, and a mutation under it left them
naming freed nodes. Taffy still visits a hidden box's children and
hoisted boxes (hidden layout, rounding), and paint its paint children:
"invalid SlotMap key used" at node_from_id, or an unwrap in paint.

Damage propagation, which visits every restyled node, now has a box
whose display is none forget all of that, for itself and its former
subtree, freeing their anonymous blocks. Shown again, the subtree is
styled and constructed afresh. In debug builds,
assert_layout_parents_consistent held no more after such a mutation;
it holds again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
